# Cursor rules: AI context

Always read and follow the shared context first:

- `ai-context/_shared/README.md`
- `ai-context/task-details.md`
- `ai-context/frontend-skills/` (when working on UI)

Only then apply any Cursor-specific behavior/preferences.

When adding/changing rules:
- Put canonical rules in `ai-context/_shared/README.md`
- Keep this file as a thin pointer + any Cursor-only overrides

## Playwright MCP (local URLs)

When calling **`user-playwright`** tools (`browser_navigate`, snapshots, clicks, etc.) against this project’s dev servers, use **`http://localhost:`** plus the port (e.g. `http://localhost:5173`, `http://localhost:3000`), **not** `127.0.0.1`.
